  "rationale": [
    "One active OpenCut architecture decision: CFA3-native FAST EDIT / QuickClip with standalone and Webdesign-embedded surfaces, not a full NLE.",
    "Shared Programmable Video Editing Fabric serves Video Editor, OpenCut, OpenVid Shared, QuickClip and adapters without a separate editing/motion authority.",
    "OpenTimelineIO is interchange only; CFA3-native application project state remains authoritative, and the CFA3 Video Editor alone provides full NLE.",
    "OpenCut upstream is an optional architectural/API/plugin/headless/scripting/MCP/UI-independent reference with runtime admission still fail-closed.",
    "Historical 2026-09-01 decision is embedded without alteration in historical_decision; historical CI evidence remains immutable.",
    "Shared MLT or CFA3 Native Media Composition execution uses CFA3-wide shared FFmpeg; fixed capability baseline stays 175."
  ],
